[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5952452312","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124090#issuecomment-5952452312","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124090","id":5952452312,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYss22A","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T12:35:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T12:59:20Z","body":"In SVG polylines, sharp angles are dealt with by having a miterlimit, if your miter gets too big, it falls back to bevel. We seem to be instead clamping the miter and tanking the non-uniform width, which goes against the documentation and looks bad. In my opinion, if we don't add more control to the method, it should either properly handle miterlimits or bevel instead.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5952452312/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":nul